<title>UK: H&amp;C Furnishings driven by consumer buoyancy.</title>
<headline>H&amp;C Furnishings driven by consumer buoyancy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to April 26, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		12.58		  vs 2.12</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)   6.0		  vs 3.0</p>
<p> Pretax			 8.2		  vs 0.437</p>
<p> Turnover		   151.8		  vs 60.9</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said current trading was benefiting from consumer spending. Like-for-like sales were up 13 percent in the first ten weeks of the current year. The company's figures include nine months trading by Harvey's following the group's merger.</p>
<p>Full company name - H &amp; C Furnishings Plc</p>
